+ * coordinates, evaluated in double precision, so with tolerances of 0 the
+ * test is exact and a point on the boundary is inside. A chromaticity inside
+ * the triangle is a non-negative combination of the three primaries, so it
+ * has no negative component in linear RGB of @outer. @outer must not be
+ * collinear.
